      "content": "14|But one detail disturbed the people of [[Doobius House]] more than any other.\n15|\n16|He swore that after his companions died, **he could still hear them screaming from inside the tomb.**\n17|\n18|The tomb is the hidden laboratory of **[[Dopendis Gravebreath]]**, a necromancer and arcanist of [[Orcus]] who discovered a means of capturing mortal souls and storing them within enchanted vessels. Dopendis Gravebreath was supplied by a hidden Orcus cult operating among Stickyickistan’s mining interests; the cult sought to turn the island’s abundant [[Arcanite]] into a power source for a mass raise dead ritual.\n19|\n20|Dopendis Gravebreath has disappeared.\n21|\n22|His experiments have not.\n23|\n24|---\n25|\n26|# Adventure Hook\n27|\n28|The characters hear about the tomb while staying in [[Doobius House]].\n29|\n30|Several families are desperate to learn what happened to the missing explorers. A local scholar from the [[Seekers of the Vein]] is equally interested in the strange structure: the old service road once connected to [[Blacklung Quarry]], and the tomb’s stonework contains traces of refined [[Arcanite]]. The scholar offers the characters **100 gp** if they can determine the structure’s purpose and return with evidence.\n31|\n32|The sole survivor, **Bongston Vale**, can also be questioned.\n33|\n34|Bongston remembers little clearly, but repeatedly warns:\n35|\n36|> \"Don't touch the jars. Gods above, don't touch the jars.\"",
