      "content": "24|---\n25|\n26|# Adventure Hook\n27|\n28|The characters begin at the [[FLS Guildhall]] on [[Nevercough Island]], looking for discreet work in [[The Roach Clip]]. A folded notice tucked inside the latest edition reads:\n29|\n30|> **Missing explorers. Quiet recovery job. Tomb in the wooded interior near [[Doobius House]]. Find out what happened, retrieve any remains or personal effects, and bring back anything that explains the jars. Ask no authorities. Payment: 100 gp.**\n31|\n32|The notice was posted by an anonymous patron claiming to represent the families of the missing adventurers. It avoids naming the tomb’s sponsor, but promises an additional payment if the characters recover evidence about the refined [[Arcanite]] found in its stonework. The job is unofficial, and the patron makes clear that the [[Free League of Stickyickistan]] is not responsible for the contract.\n33|\n34|The sole survivor, **Bongston Vale**, is recovering in the guildhall’s [[FLS Guildhall#Recovery support|recovery quarters]]. The characters can question him before leaving, but he remembers little clearly and repeatedly warns:\n35|\n36|> \"Don't touch the jars. Gods above, don't touch the jars.\"\n37|\n38|He remembers seeing his companions die—and then hearing their voices begging him for help from somewhere deeper inside the tomb.\n39|\n40|---\n41|\n42|# Reaching the Tomb\n43|\n44|The tomb lies roughly **two days from [[Doobius House]]** through dense forest.\n45|\n46|The journey doesn't need to be a full wilderness adventure. Instead, use it to establish the increasingly unnatural atmosphere surrounding the tomb.\n47|\n48|During the second day, animals become scarce.\n49|\n50|Birdsong disappears.\n51|\n52|That evening, characters occasionally hear whispers between the trees.\n53|\n54|A character who succeeds on a **DC 12 Wisdom (Perception)** check hears fragments:\n55|\n56|_\"Come closer...\"_\n57|\n58|_\"It hurts...\"_\n59|\n60|_\"Please...\"_\n61|\n62|_\"There's room for you too...\"_\n63|\n64|These aren't ghosts wandering the forest. They are psychic echoes emanating from the Jars of Souls.\n65|",
