      "content": "24|---\n25|\n26|# Adventure Hook\n27|\n28|The characters begin at the [[FLS Guildhall]] on [[Nevercough Island]], looking for work through the [[Free League of Stickyickistan]]. A public notice on [[The Rolling Papers]] offers **100 gp** to investigate a newly revealed tomb in the wooded interior of [[The Outback]] and return with evidence of its purpose.\n29|\n30|The notice was posted by a scholar working with [[The Seekers of the Vein]]. The scholar believes the tomb’s stonework contains traces of refined [[Arcanite]], suggesting that someone transported valuable material deep into the forest. Several families from [[Doobius House]] have also contacted the Guildhall, desperate to learn what happened to the missing explorers.\n31|\n32|The sole survivor, **Bongston Vale**, is recovering in the guildhall’s [[FLS Guildhall#Recovery support|recovery quarters]] and can be questioned before the party leaves. Bongston remembers little clearly, but repeatedly warns:\n33|\n34|> \"Don't touch the jars. Gods above, don't touch the jars.\"\n35|\n36|He remembers seeing his companions die—and then hearing their voices begging him for help from somewhere deeper inside the tomb.\n37|\n38|## The Roach Clip Hook: Unfinished Business\n39|\n40|Characters who took part in [[The Tenebrous Stone-r]] may find a second notice in [[The Roach Clip]], tucked behind the public posting or passed to them by a quiet Guildhall contact. The coded notice reads:\n41|\n42|> **The mountain’s dead are still being moved. Find the missing shipment before it reaches the forest. Ask about the jars. Tell no one in a uniform.**\n43|\n44|The Roach Clip contact believes the tomb is connected to the same Orcus cult and soul-powered experiments encountered beneath [[Blacklung Quarry]]. The party is asked to determine whether the cult is still operating, recover evidence, and prevent the shipment from reaching another site.\n45|\n46|This hook is ideal for returning characters from [[The Tenebrous Stone-r]]. They may recognize the cult’s methods, the smell of corrupted [[Arcannabis]], or the traces of Arcanite used in the tomb’s construction. The public 100 gp reward remains available, but the Roach Clip contact offers an additional **100 gp** for keeping the connection to [[Blacklung Quarry]] quiet or recovering a usable cult insignia, soul-storage component, or other evidence.\n47|\n48|---\n49|\n50|# Reaching the Tomb\n51|\n52|The tomb lies roughly **two days from [[Doobius House]]** through dense forest.\n53|\n54|The journey doesn't need to be a full wilderness adventure. Instead, use it to establish the increasingly unnatural atmosphere surrounding the tomb.\n55|\n56|During the second day, animals become scarce.\n57|\n58|Birdsong disappears.\n59|\n60|That evening, characters occasionally hear whispers between the trees.\n61|\n62|A character who succeeds on a **DC 12 Wisdom (Perception)** check hears fragments:\n63|\n64|_\"Come closer...\"_\n65|",
