      "content": "44|> **Job: Recover the black soul-jars from the tomb beyond [[Doobius House]]. Bring back every jar you find, fully intact. Do not open, smash, or hand them to the authorities. Payment is 300 gp per jar at the Dungsweepers’ mortuary in [[The Undercity Osslurraggath]]. Use the key phrase \"The dead are still moving\" to collect reward.**\n45|\n46|The contact is [[Skarguther Dungleboof]], a well-connected member of the [[Heralds of Dust]], CFO of the Stickyickistanian [[Dungsweepers]], and collector of cursed relics. He believes the jars are linked to the Orcus cult beneath [[Blacklung Quarry]] and wants them recovered intact—not to fuel another ritual, but to remove the tortured souls from the cult’s reach and study how they might be guided toward [[Heralds of Dust|True Death]]. His methods are unofficial and sometimes illegal, but he is not necessarily malicious.\n47|\n48|> **“Touch the jars. Bring me every one you can carry.”**\n49|\n50|Skarguther pays **600 gp per intact jar**, up to **1,200 gp** for the two active jars in the ritual chamber. To collect, deliver the jars to the Dungsweepers’ mortuary offices in [[The Undercity Osslurraggath]] and give the clerk the notice or the phrase **“The dead are still moving.”** Broken jars and released souls earn no payment. The public 100 gp reward remains available, but this contract asks the characters to collect the jars rather than smash them.\n51|\n52|---\n53|\n54|# Reaching the Tomb\n55|\n56|The tomb lies roughly **two days from [[Doobius House]]** through dense forest.",
