{"path":"content/Adventures/DM Notes/FLS/Tier 1/Jars of Souls.md","oldText":"Destroying the jar releases the souls trapped inside. A wave of spectral energy fills the chamber, and every creature within 10 feet must make a **DC 12 Wisdom saving throw**. On a failure, the creature is **Frightened until the end of its next turn**.

The spirits then disappear. A character proficient in Arcana or Religion realizes that the souls have finally been allowed to pass into the afterlife.","newText":"Destroying the jar releases the souls trapped inside. A violent wave of spectral energy fills the chamber. Every creature within 10 feet must make a **DC 12 Wisdom saving throw**, taking **2d6 Psychic damage** on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature that fails the save is also **Frightened for 1 minute**. The creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.

Outside combat, the effect lasts long enough to matter: a frightened character may flee the chamber, drop what they are carrying, or be unable to approach another jar until they recover. The spirits then disappear. A character proficient in Arcana or Religion realizes that the souls have finally been allowed to pass into the afterlife."}

{"path":"content/Adventures/DM Notes/FLS/Tier 1/Jars of Souls.md","oldText":"Destroying the jar releases the souls trapped inside. A wave of spectral energy fills the chamber, and every creature within 10 feet must make a **DC 12 Wisdom saving throw**. On a failure, the creature is **Frightened until the end of its next turn**.

The spirits then disappear. A character proficient in Arcana or Religion realizes that the souls have finally been allowed to pass into the afterlife.","newText":"Destroying the jar releases the souls trapped inside. A violent wave of spectral energy fills the chamber. Every creature within 10 feet must make a **DC 12 Wisdom saving throw**, taking **2d6 Psychic damage** on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature that fails the save is also **Frightened for 1 minute**. The creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.

Outside combat, the effect lasts long enough to matter: a frightened character may flee the chamber, drop what they are carrying, or be unable to approach another jar until they recover. The spirits then disappear. A character proficient in Arcana or Religion realizes that the souls have finally been allowed to pass into the afterlife."}

