      "hasMoreBelow": true,
      "nextStartLine": 154,
      "content": "120|---\n121|\n122|# 3. Immortal Guardians\n123|\n124|Two separate chambers contain one of Dopendis Gravebreath's earliest successful Jars of Souls each. These two jars are **inert**: they contain tortured souls, but they do not power the tomb's guardians or emit necrotic energy.\n125|\n126|Each room contains:\n127|\n128|- Two stone guardian statues\n129|- One inert Jar of Souls\n130|- Ancient necromantic inscriptions\n131|\n132|When a creature approaches within 10 feet of the jar, the statues animate.\n133|\n134|### Encounter\n135|\n136|Use **2 Animated Armors** in each room.\n137|\n138|However, the guardians aren't interested in pursuing intruders through the dungeon.\n139|\n140|They exist solely to protect the jar.\n141|\n142|If characters retreat from the chamber, the constructs return to their original positions after 1 minute.\n143|\n144|### The Jar\n145|\n146|A black ceramic vessel rests upon a stone pedestal. Ghostly faces occasionally push outward from its surface before disappearing.\n147|\n148|Each jar contains several tortured souls, the voices Bongston heard after his companions died. A creature that touches the jar hears dozens of overlapping whispers, including fragments of the souls’ final memories.\n149|\n150|Characters who accepted [[Skarguther Dungleboof]]’s [[The Roach Clip]] contract can identify this as the item he wants. He pays **600 gp for each intact jar**, whether it is one of these two inert vessels or one of the four active jars in the ritual chamber. The vessel must remain sealed and undamaged; a broken jar earns nothing. Characters who did not accept the contract can still recognize that the jar would interest collectors of forbidden magic, but selling it would be dangerous and morally fraught.\n151|\n152|This creates a clear choice. The characters can carry the jar to Skarguther, placing its tortured souls in the hands of a Duster who claims he can guide them toward [[Heralds of Dust|True Death]]. Or they can smash it, freeing the souls and allowing them to pass into the afterlife, but destroying the vessel and forfeiting its reward. They may choose differently for each jar, but Skarguther pays only for intact vessels.\n153|",
