      "content": "144|### The Inert Jar\n145|\n146|A black ceramic vessel rests upon a stone pedestal. Ghostly faces occasionally push outward from its surface before disappearing.\n147|\n148|Each inert jar contains several tortured souls, the voices Bongston heard after his companions died. A creature that touches the jar hears dozens of overlapping whispers, including fragments of the souls’ final memories. Unlike the active jars in Area 7, an inert jar is not connected to the ritual machinery and does not empower the undead.\n149|\n150|Characters who accepted [[Skarguther Dungleboof]]’s [[The Roach Clip]] contract can identify this as the item he wants. He pays **100 gp for each intact inert jar** in Area 3 and **300 gp for each intact active jar** in the ritual chamber. The vessel must remain sealed and undamaged; a broken jar earns nothing. Characters who did not accept the contract can still recognize that the jar would interest collectors of forbidden magic, but selling it would be dangerous and morally fraught.\n151|\n152|This creates a clear choice. The characters can carry the jar to Skarguther, placing its tortured souls in the hands of a Duster who claims he can guide them toward [[Heralds of Dust|True Death]]. Or they can smash it, freeing the souls and allowing them to pass into the afterlife, but destroying the vessel and forfeiting its reward. They may choose differently for each jar, but Skarguther pays only for intact vessels.\n153|\n154|### Breaking an Inert Jar\n155|\n156|AC 12  \n157|HP 10  \n158|Immune: Poison, Psychic\n159|\n160|Destroying an inert jar releases the souls trapped inside, but because the vessel is disconnected from the ritual machinery, it does not produce the violent psychic backlash of an active jar. The spirits emerge as pale figures, briefly surround the characters, and then disappear. A character proficient in Arcana or Religion realizes that the souls have finally been allowed to pass into the afterlife.\n161|\n162|### Taking the Jar\n163|\n164|The characters may instead carry the intact vessel. It is heavy, fragile, and constantly whispers to anyone holding it. Wrapping it securely prevents accidental damage, but does not silence the voices.\n165|\n166|If the characters accepted Skarguther’s contract, they must transport the jar to the Dungsweepers’ mortuary offices in [[The Undercity Osslurraggath]] and present it to Skarguther or one of his Duster attendants to collect the reward. Otherwise, carrying it could attract the attention of necromancers, undead creatures, religious authorities, or [[Dopendis Gravebreath]].",
