      "content": "386|A character who spends 10 minutes examining an active jar and succeeds on a **DC 14 Intelligence (Arcana or Nature)** check realizes that the vessels are distilling Soul Diesel: trapped souls mixed with humanoid blood and refined into a potent Arcannabis concentrate.\n387|\n388|The strain’s spiritual energy can be transferred into another ritual or magical object. A creature that ingests it gains **1d4 bonus damage of the same type as its attack against humanoids** for 1 hour, with the bonus applying once per turn. Whatever Dopendis Gravebreath intended to do here required an enormous amount of Soul Diesel.\n389|\n390|### Soul Diesel and the Orcus Cult\n391|\n392|A character who succeeds on a **DC 14 Intelligence (Arcana or Nature)** check can identify the dark liquid in the active jars as **Soul Diesel**, a mixture of spiritual energy, humanoid blood, and [[Arcannabis]]. The silver wires draw the mixture from the jars and feed it into the undead guardians.\n393|\n394|Near the ritual platform, the characters find a folded note sealed with the same crude open-hand-and-skull mark seen beneath [[Blacklung Quarry]]. It reads:\n395|\n396|> **The mountain operation is lost. The forest laboratory remains viable. Continue the Soul Diesel process here and await further instructions. Do not allow the vessels to be opened.**\n397|\n398|A character who has participated in [[The Tenebrous Stone-r]] recognizes the seal. The note confirms that the quarry and this tomb were separate sites used by the same Orcus cult, without suggesting that they produced the same Arcannabis strain.",
