      "content": "20|## Adventure Hook\n21|\n22|The characters begin at the [[FLS Guildhall]] on [[Nevercough Island]]. The job appears on [[The Rolling Papers]] as a public recovery contract, though the payment comes from several interested parties.\n23|\n24|> **MISSING CARGO: A sealed wagon disappeared on the forest road after leaving [[Doobius House]]. Recover the wagon, identify the thieves, and return any surviving cargo to the Guildhall. Payment: 500 gp each, plus documented bonuses for recovered evidence and rescued travelers.**\n25|\n26|The contract was posted by a clerk working with [[The Seekers of the Vein]]. The Seekers want their equipment returned, but they are not the only people interested in the missing wagon.\n27|\n28|When the characters open the damaged crates, a puff of foul-smelling [[Arcannabis]] smoke escapes. Characters who completed [[The Tenebrous Stone-r]] recognize it as the same kind of smoke that drifted from [[Blacklung Quarry]].\n29|\n30|> “If the cargo contains soul vessels, do not let the authorities break them open in a warehouse. Bring me the ledger. Bring me the names. If there are souls involved, bring me proof that they are free.”\n31|\n32|Skarguther offers an additional **200 gp** for the Ash Ledger and asks the characters to report whether the shipment contained living captives or trapped souls. He does not ask them to steal or preserve any soul vessels for his collection. He wants information about the cult’s activities and the location of any remaining prisoners.",
