      "content": "145|\n146|The cult fanatic tries to destroy the maps and the ledger before fighting to the death. The animated armor protects the Soul Diesel equipment.\n147|\n148|If the characters rescue the prisoners, award the optional rescue XP listed in the rewards section.\n149|\n150|### The Ash Ledger\n151|\n152|The Ash Ledger is a black leather notebook bound with wire. Its pages are written in three inks: red for names, black for payments, and green for Arcannabis shipments.\n153|\n154|The ledger contains:\n155|\n156|- Payments to a supplier near [[Blacklung Quarry]].\n157|- A note describing the forest laboratory as “Dopendis’s abandoned refinement site.”\n158|- A reference to the failed quarry operation.\n159|- A list of surviving cult contacts.\n160|- A final page describing the waterworks ritual.\n161|\n162|The ledger does not identify the Orcus cult’s ultimate leader. It does identify enough suppliers and messengers to prove that the quarry operation and the Soul Diesel laboratory belonged to the same broader network.\n163|\n164|A character who studies the ledger for 10 minutes can identify a name connected to their past adventures. Choose one:\n165|\n166|- A quarry worker who escaped the events of [[The Tenebrous Stone-r]].\n167|- A cult courier who visited the tomb in [[Jars of Souls]].\n168|- A supplier who sold equipment through an otherwise legitimate business.\n169|\n170|## Part 4: The Old Waterworks",
